.venv/
__pycache__/
.env
.CLAUDE.md
build/
src/model/

# data/ splits in two, and the split is the rule rather than a list of exceptions.
#
#   RAW COLLECTED DATA is never committed. Raw XML, parsed Parquet, live poll output,
#   snapshots. It is large, it is reproducible by re-fetching, and it is not the repo's job.
#
#   SMALL DERIVED ARTIFACTS REQUIRED TO BUILD OR REPRODUCE are committed. Without them a
#   fresh clone cannot produce a deployable package, which was true until 2026-08-31 and
#   was found by cloning and running the build rather than by reading this file.
#
# Everything under data/ is ignored by default; each exception below is deliberate and
# says what breaks without it. Note `data/*` rather than `data/`: git does not descend
# into an excluded directory, so a bare `data/` would make every negation below silently
# inert -- which it was, and the one file that got in did so via `git add -f`.
data/*

# 228 KB. Every train code ever observed, from a harvest that cannot be repeated for the
# past. Read by backfill.py and validate_join.py.
!data/codes.json

# 12 KB. The station list. build_lambda.ps1 and build_api.ps1 both throw without it.
!data/live/
data/live/*
!data/live/stations.json

# ~1.1 MB per version. The model that build_api.ps1 bakes into the Lambda package, so a
# clone cannot build a deployable API without it. Committing every version also means the
# exact artifact behind any published figure is recoverable, which the accuracy page's
# claims depend on. Retraining is not scheduled (see CLAUDE.md), so this grows rarely.
!data/models/
